Verify the device generates a log when login events occur.
[edit] show system syslog host { any <info | any>;
source-address ;
} If an external syslog host is not configured to log, or configured for facility any severity <info | any>, this is a finding.

Verify the device generates a log when login events occur.
[edit] show system syslog host { any any;
source-address ;
} If an external syslog host is not configured to log, or configured for facility any severity any, this is a finding.

Verify the device generates a log when login events occur.
[edit] show system syslog host { any any;
source-address ;
} If an external syslog host is not configured to log, or configured for facility any severity any, this is a finding.

Verify only a single local account has an authentication stanza and that the name is the account of last resort.
[edit] show system login user { uid 2001;
class ;
authentication { <--- This stanza permits local login encrypted-password "$sha2$22895$aVBPaRVa$o6xIqNSYg9D7yt8pI47etAjZV9uuwHrhAFT6R021HNsy";
## SECRET-DATA } } OR user { uid 2001;
class ;
} If accounts other than the account of last resort contain an authentication stanza, and that account is not documented, this is a finding.
